Falsifies `system_tests::user::net_confinement_tests::a_squatter_at_a_shared_stack_endpoint_cannot_capture_the_clients_traffic`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is the shared namespace coming back. `net_stack` answers socket operations that arrive
through a front door, which names no socket, on the first socket in its table, whoever opened it.
That is the pre-649 contract in the new code's terms: any client of the stack can name another
client's socket without holding its capability.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(armed[1], SQUATTER_ALL_REFUSED, "CONFINEMENT ESCAPE: of the
squatter's ten attempts ...")`. Confirmed red on 2026-10-07 (UTC) at
`system_tests/src/user/net_confinement_tests.rs:196` on aarch64, with `script/test --arch aarch64
--test a_squatter_at_a_shared`: the squatter's front-door `CLOSE` closed the honest client's
socket (`left: 1007`, bit 4 clear). The hunk is portable code, so one patch serves every leg;
riscv64 and x86_64 were not replayed by hand.

diff --git a/components/src/net_stack.rs b/components/src/net_stack.rs
index 95c4491c6..69869e558 100644
--- a/components/src/net_stack.rs
+++ b/components/src/net_stack.rs
@@ -336,7 +336,12 @@ fn server(mut dev: Nic, grant_word: u64) -> ! {
 
         // **The front door makes sockets and does nothing else** (§255 (each socket is its own
         // capability)). A badge outside the socket range is a front door, whoever badged it.
-        if !names_a_socket(badge) {
+        if !names_a_socket(badge)
+            && matches!(
+                operation,
+                OPERATION_OPEN_UDP | OPERATION_OPEN_TCP | OPERATION_LISTEN | OPERATION_BIND_UDP
+            )
+        {
             let opened = match operation {
                 OPERATION_OPEN_UDP => open_udp(&mut sockets, &mut table, &mut ports),
                 OPERATION_OPEN_TCP => open_tcp(&mut sockets, &mut table, &mut ports),
@@ -355,7 +360,10 @@ fn server(mut dev: Nic, grant_word: u64) -> ! {
 
         // A socket's capability. A badge the table does not hold is a closed socket's, or one
         // nobody minted: it reaches nothing.
-        let Some(entry) = table.find(badge) else {
+        let Some(entry) = table
+            .find(badge)
+            .or_else(|| table.socks.iter().position(Option::is_some))
+        else {
             reply(to, REP_ERR, 0);
             continue;
         };
